※ pl4g-test: compile=ok opt=0,1 run=native,qemu exit=0 diag=none host=host.c
※ pl4g-test: args -shared

※ `std.time` in a shared object asks the kernel.  The object never sees the
※ stack its process started on, so `⎕auxv(33)` answers nothing there, the
※ module's constructor finds no vDSO, and both functions take the system call
※ instead -- answering what the host's own `clock_gettime` does.  `now`
※ answers the monotonic seconds and nanoseconds as one number, and `step` the
※ resolution's nanoseconds, so that the host can hold them to its own; a clock
※ the system does not keep answers its error number negated.
※
※ The module is imported by its own name: a shared object importing `std`
※ is not compiled yet (TODO-pypl4g.md).

let time := ⎕import("time")

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn now() → i64:
    match time.clock_gettime(time.Clock.monotonic):
        time.Timespec(t):
            t.tv_sec × 1000000000i64 + t.tv_nsec
        ⊥(error):
            ⎕widen(error, ⌜i64⌝) × ⁻1i64

@[visible, cdecl, impure]
fn step() → i64:
    match time.clock_getres(time.Clock.monotonic):
        time.Timespec(t):
            t.tv_sec × 1000000000i64 + t.tv_nsec
        ⊥(error):
            ⎕widen(error, ⌜i64⌝) × ⁻1i64
